body:
1) n2_apple.h has no HEVC parameter-set calls. To build the 'hvc1' format description I need:
  OSStatus CMVideoFormatDescriptionCreateFromHEVCParameterSets(CFAllocatorRef, size_t parameterSetCount,
      const uint8_t *const *parameterSetPointers, const size_t *parameterSetSizes, int NALUnitHeaderLength,
      CFDictionaryRef extensions, CMFormatDescriptionRef *formatDescriptionOut);
  OSStatus CMVideoFormatDescriptionGetHEVCParameterSetAtIndex(CMFormatDescriptionRef, size_t index,
      const uint8_t **ps, size_t *size, size_t *count, int *nalUnitHeaderLength);
They are public CoreMedia API (same family as the H.264 calls already in n2_apple.h). Proposal: add them to gpu/video/include/n2_apple.h (you) and to gpu/video/fake/fake_apple.c (WP02) so every host test gets them. Until then I declare them in my own vt/n2hwenc_vt.h, list them in vt/symbols.txt, and provide test-local implementations in vt/test/t_support.c for the host suite (the real symbols exist on iOS). No workaround in the object code; it calls the real API. Do you want the header text posted to the gpu/video owner instead?

2) Fallback when vcodecd is unreachable at StartSession. Proposal: return kVTVideoEncoderNotAvailableNowErr = -12915 (public VTErrors.h, value read from the SDK in gpu/build/apple-toolchain/sdks/iPhoneOS16.5.sdk). Reasoning: the selection loop is documented as trying the next candidate when one cannot be created/started; -12915 is the status whose documented meaning is exactly 'encoder not available now', so VideoToolbox can skip to the software object registered for the same codec ('avc1' n2avc, 'hvc1' Apple's VCPHEVC), which stays registered and is what n2avc_vt.c is. I could not verify in the cache which statuses the loop retries on: gpu/video/research/dis.py needs allsyms.pkl (absent here) and the cache header does not match cachetools/dsc2.py, so this is [I] from the documented meaning and the lead's loop note in gpu/video/PLAN.md section 1.3, not [V]. Belt and braces: I also export n2hwenc_vt_available(), a non-blocking probe that the registration hook can use so we do not register the object at all when vcodecd is absent (post to hw-ip with the exact call). Does that match your intent, or do you have a verified status code/retry list to use instead?

Registration (deliverable): ImplementationID stays ours (N2VT_ID_AVC for 'avc1', a new com.nord2.videotoolbox.videoencoder.hvc1.n2hw for 'hvc1'), IsHardwareAccelerated=true, Rating=100 (software objects are registered without a rating, i.e. 0). Since n2vt_shim.c is read-only for me, vt/n2hwenc_register.c exposes N2HWENC_Register(void) and I will post the exact 2-line weak-symbol call to add to SLIMEncoderRegister for you/hw-ip.
